  "query_preview": "..\nSYNOPTIC SETUP:\n\nLarge upper low over the Gulf of Alaska will keep the upper flow \nover our area into Friday generally from the SW.\n\nA disturbance moving NE out of eastern Idaho has tapped into\na deep monsoonal moisture plumb. This disturbance will spread \nshowers and thunderstorms northeast across mainly the SE zones \nthis morning, with some areas potentially picking up over .25\".\n\nThis system will move out later Wednesday allowing things to heat\nup a bit for Thursday. This should be the warmest day this week\nwith highs in the upper 70s and 80s.\n\nA vigorous upper trough will then swing east through the Pacific \nNW Friday. With a surface low over western/central Montana, \nsoutherly winds will increase over our CWA for a likelihood of a \nLake Wind Advisory.\n\nOn Saturday, a strong surface low will move NE into central Sask\nbringing a cold front through early followed by windy conditions \nto the CWA. Temperatures will drop back close to normal levels. \nLake Wind Advisory will be likely needed but winds should drop off\nSaturday evening.\n\nA nearly zonal flow will keep temps near normal into next week\nwhile a disturbance looks to pass to our south. Showers are\npossible Sunday night through Monday night. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nDid not see any glaring reasons to deviate from the NBM. TFJ",
